        System.out.println(k.open);
        System.out.println(k.owner);
    }
}
```

The four printlns give `0 / 0.0 / false / null`.

The statement **Parcel p;** only declares a reference variable; no object exists, so no constructor runs. The statement **p = new Parcel();** creates the object and runs the constructor.

```java
